+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are the `apiKeys`
+in the data file (`docs/DATA.md`). Without a key, or with an unknown one,
+the answer is 401 `unauthorized`; with a key whose role does not allow the
+request it is 403 `forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: the same, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request with a known key and a method other than `GET` writes an audit
+entry, whatever its outcome (refused and failed requests too):
+`{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`. `GET /audit` (managers only)
+lists them newest first.
+
